## 15. Important scope rule

When resolving a reference inside a Library, candidate search should normally be restricted to:

```text
current block
current Library
current Library interfaces
project-level objects
top-level Data Sources / Data Sets
explicitly exposed Outputs from another Library
```

Do NOT search internal fields of every other Library.

This is especially important for common short names such as:

```text
rate
time
spot
value
index
```

---

## 16. NPZ safety and performance

Do not expand every Data Source row or array element.

Only extract schema-level information:

- container
- fields
- dtype
- shape

If object arrays require special handling, isolate that logic clearly.

Avoid enabling unsafe pickle loading unless it is actually required by the trusted internal NPZ format.

---

